  "description": "Self-shifting transmissions using epicyclic (planetary) gearsets, hydraulic torque converters, and clutched brake bands or multidisc packs. Ratios changed automatically by governor pressure, valve body logic, or electronic control units. 4-9 forward speeds; the dominant passenger-car transmission since the 1950s. Torque converter multiplies engine torque 2-2.5x at stall.",
